  <section class="section" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
    <div class="conteneur">
      <div class="mesure-lecture">

        <h2 id="features-title">What it does</h2>
        <p>
          You ask your assistant a question as usual. When it is about a character or a keyboard layout, the
          assistant calls AZERTY Coach and answers with the keys to press.
        </p>
        <p>Examples of questions:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>“How do I type a capital É on my keyboard?”</li>
          <li>“How do I write French quotation marks?”</li>
          <li>“I’m moving from a US keyboard to an AZERTY: which keys will change?”</li>
          <li>“Give me an exercise to learn AZERTY Global, then check what I typed.”</li>
        </ul>
        <p>AZERTY Coach gives the assistant five tools:</p>
        <dl class="fiches">
          <dt class="fiches__nom">Find a character</dt>
          <dd class="fiches__quoi">From the character, its name or a description (“o and e joined”), gives the keys to press, the recommended method and, when there is one, another method (an Alt code on Windows, a character to copy).</dd>

          <dt class="fiches__nom">Type a short text</dt>
          <dd class="fiches__quoi">For each character beyond plain letters, says how to type it, and flags the ones that cannot be typed on the chosen layout.</dd>

          <dt class="fiches__nom">Compare two layouts</dt>
          <dd class="fiches__quoi">Lists the keys that change between a starting layout and a target layout, from the most frequent to the rarest.</dd>

          <dt class="fiches__nom">Browse the lessons</dt>
          <dd class="fiches__quoi">Gives the AZERTY Global lessons and exercises, to read or to do.</dd>

          <dt class="fiches__nom">Check an exercise</dt>
          <dd class="fiches__quoi">Compares what you typed with the exercise and shows the differences character by character, including the ’ apostrophe, the non-breaking space and accented capitals.</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>
          Depending on the application, the answer may come with a visual keyboard that circles the keys to
          press. Without it, the answer stays text.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="setup" aria-labelledby="setup-title">
    <div class="conteneur">
      <div class="mesure-lecture">

        <h2 id="setup-title">Setup</h2>
        <p>
          In all three cases you add the same server by its address, with no account and no key:
        </p>
        <p><code>{{ mesure.coach.url }}</code></p>
        <p>
          Menu names change with your plan and the version of the application: the steps below follow each
          publisher’s documentation.
        </p>

        <h3 id="setup-claude">In Claude</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Open Claude’s settings, in the connectors section.</li>
          <li>Choose “Add custom connector”.</li>
          <li>Name it “AZERTY Coach” and paste the address above.</li>
          <li>Confirm. No sign-in is requested.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          On a Team or Enterprise plan, the organization owner adds the connector; members can then use it.
        </p>

        <h3 id="setup-chatgpt">In ChatGPT</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>In settings, in the connectors section, turn on developer mode (advanced settings).</li>
          <li>Create a connector, name it “AZERTY Coach” and paste the address above.</li>
          <li>Choose “No authentication”, confirm that you trust the connector, then create it.</li>
          <li>In a conversation, add AZERTY Coach from the tools menu.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Developer mode depends on your plan: in a Business, Enterprise or Education workspace, an
          administrator must allow it first.
        </p>

        <h3 id="setup-codex">In Codex</h3>
        <p>Add these lines to the <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> file, then restart Codex:</p>
<pre><code>[mcp_servers.azerty-coach]
url = "{{ mesure.coach.url }}"</code></pre>
        <p>
          In the Codex app, you can also add it from the MCP server settings.
        </p>

        <h3 id="setup-remove">To remove it</h3>
        <p>
          Delete the connector in the same settings (or remove the two lines from <code>config.toml</code>).
          Nothing is installed on your computer: there is nothing else to uninstall.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <div class="conteneur">
      <div class="mesure-lecture">

        <h2 id="limits-title">Limits</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Read-only.</strong> AZERTY Coach explains; it types nothing for you and acts on no software.</li>
          <li><strong>Layouts covered.</strong> AZERTY Global, plus a few other layouts checked one by one. For a layout it does not have, it does not guess: it says so.</li>
          <li><strong>Short texts.</strong> The tools take a character, a sentence or a small exercise, not a document.</li>
          <li><strong>The assistant words its own answer.</strong> It rephrases what AZERTY Coach returns. If in doubt, try the key combination given.</li>
          <li><strong>Availability.</strong> The service is free and comes with no availability commitment; see the <a href="/en/azerty-coach-terms">terms of use</a>.</li>
        </ul>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="support" aria-labelledby="support-title">
    <div class="conteneur">
      <div class="mesure-lecture">

        <h2 id="support-title">Support</h2>
        <p>
          A mistake in an answer, a connector that will not add, a missing layout: write to
          <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:{{ mesure.coach.contactSupport }}">{{ mesure.coach.contactSupport }}</a><!--/email_off-->.
          Messages in French or English are both fine.
        </p>
        <p>So that we can reproduce the problem, tell us:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>the assistant you used (Claude, ChatGPT or Codex) and your system;</li>
          <li>the question you asked and the answer you got;</li>
          <li>the character or layout concerned.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Please do not send personal information: it is not needed. If your question is about your data,
          write to the same address and say so.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

